{
  "requirement": "Habeas MUST define its authoring configuration using these data structures:\n\n```text\nUserAuthoringConfig {\n    default: Optional<ConfigName>,\n    configs: Map<ConfigName, AuthoringConfig>,\n    projects: Map<CanonicalProjectRoot, ProjectSelection>,\n}\n\nProjectSelection {\n    config: ConfigName,\n}\n\nAuthoringConfig {\n    backend: BackendConfig,                   // tagged union, flattened in TOML\n    concurrency: Optional<PositiveInteger>,   // simultaneous assessments\n}\n\nBackendConfig = Bedrock(BedrockConfig) | Ollama(OllamaConfig)\n\nBedrockConfig {\n    model: ModelId,                           // model ID or inference-profile ID/ARN\n    aws_profile: Optional<String>,\n    region: Optional<String>,\n    options: Map<String, OptionValue>,\n}\n\nOllamaConfig {\n    model: ModelId,                           // exact identifier, including tag\n    endpoint: Optional<String>,               // default: http://localhost:11434\n    api_key_env: Optional<EnvironmentVariableName>,\n    options: Map<String, OptionValue>,\n}\n\nOptionValue = String | Boolean | Integer | FiniteFloat\n            | Array<OptionValue> | Map<String, OptionValue>\n\nModelRef {\n    backend: BackendKind,                     // Bedrock or Ollama\n    model: ModelId,\n}\n```\n\n`ModelRef` MUST be derived from the selected backend configuration and MUST\npreserve the exact model identifier. It MUST identify the model without replacing\nconnection settings such as AWS profile, region, or Ollama endpoint.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The code in `src/config.rs` matches the required data structures, and the tests cover the main points of the design. I did not run the tests. I judged the serde behavior (flattened tagged enum plus `concurrency`) from reading the code and the tests' assertions.\n\n**Structure (`src/config.rs`)**\n- `UserAuthoringConfig` (lines ~25–33) has `default: Option<String>`, `configs: BTreeMap<String, AuthoringConfig>` and `projects: BTreeMap<PathBuf, ProjectSelection>`. `ProjectSelection` has `config: String`.\n- `AuthoringConfig` has `concurrency: Option<NonZeroUsize>`, so it is an optional positive integer. It has `#[serde(flatten)] backend: BackendConfig`, which is the \"tagged union, flattened in TOML\" the requirement asks for.\n- `BackendConfig` is `#[serde(tag=\"backend\", rename_all=\"lowercase\")]` with `Bedrock` and `Ollama` variants.\n- `BedrockConfig` has `model`, `aws_profile`, `region` and `options`. `OllamaConfig` has `model`, `endpoint`, `api_key_env` and `options`. The optional fields are `Option`s and are skipped on serialization when absent. `endpoint()` supplies the `http://localhost:11434` default without writing it into the saved data.\n- `OptionValue` is untagged over String, Boolean, Integer(i64), Float(f64), Array and Map. `OptionValue::validate` rejects non-finite floats recursively, which gives the \"FiniteFloat\" constraint.\n- `ModelRef { backend: BackendKind, model }` is derived by `BackendConfig::model_ref` and `ResolvedAuthoringConfig::model_ref`. It clones the exact model string and carries no profile, region or endpoint, so connection settings are not replaced.\n- Validation adds a nonempty model ID, a valid `api_key_env`, a canonical absolute project root, and rejection of option keys that would override the model, prompt or tools.\n\n**Tests (`tests/configuration.rs`)**\n- `backend_configuration_round_trips_without_materializing_defaults` parses a Bedrock config and an Ollama config.\n  - The Bedrock config has `aws_profile`, `region`, and string, float, integer, bool, array and nested-map options.\n  - It checks that the Ollama `endpoint` stays `None` while `endpoint()` returns the default.\n  - It checks `model_ref()` for the exact model `tiny:latest` and `BackendKind::Ollama`.\n  - It checks that the options JSON keeps the nested map and integer values.\n  - It checks that the serialized TOML omits `endpoint` and `concurrency`, and that parsing it again gives an equal config.\n- `authoring_concurrency_defaults_overrides_and_invalid_values` runs for both backends. It covers the absent `concurrency` case, the value 7, round-tripping, and the invalid values `0`, `-1`, `1.5` and `'2'`.\n- `explicit_project_and_default_selections_choose_whole_configs` covers `default`, the `projects` map and `ProjectSelection`.\n- `invalid_schema_and_feature_values_report_the_configuration_path` covers an empty model, an unknown field, an unsupported backend, a bad `api_key_env`, a NaN option, a reserved option key and a relative project path.\n- `ollama_authentication_resolves_separately_and_rejects_missing_values` covers `api_key_env` handling, including that the resolved secret value is never serialized.\n- `tests/authoring_cli.rs` also exercises an Ollama config end to end.\n\n**Minor gaps**\n- `model_ref()` is only asserted directly for Ollama, but the Bedrock branch is symmetric and trivial.\n- A Bedrock `ModelRef` that preserves an ARN is not asserted directly. The Bedrock TOML in the round-trip test uses an ARN, which at least exercises parsing.\n\nThere are no FIXMEs or acknowledged gaps.",
